  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ASSESSING NOVEL PATHWAYS OF MERCURY BIOACCUMULATION IN WEST AFRICAN CHIMPANZEES (PAN TROGLODYTES VERUS) IN SENEGAL</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this 2-year project is to assess the health risks that mercury usage associated with artisanal gold mining poses to western chimpanzees in Senegal. Activities include: 1) analyzing likely contaminated and uncontaminated soil and chimpanzee food samples; 2) establishing a cost-effective method of monitoring chimpanzee mercury exposure; 3) conducting a risk assessment of chimpanzee mercury poisoning; and 4) disseminating findings to the conservation community and the Senegal government to support possible mitigation actions.</narrative>
  </description>
